
# 5. BBRD — BUSINESS & BUSINESS REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT

# FixMyCampus — Business & Business Requirements Document

**Version:** 1.0
**Date:** 06 September 2026

---

# 1. Business Problem

Campus infrastructure problems may be reported through informal channels such as verbal communication or messages.

Such methods can cause:

* Lost complaints
* Delayed responses
* Lack of accountability
* Poor visibility
* Difficulty tracking resolution
* Lack of historical records

FixMyCampus addresses this problem by providing a centralized digital complaint-management process.

---

# 2. Business Objectives

The system aims to:

1. Centralize complaint reporting.
2. Improve accountability.
3. Improve complaint visibility.
4. Establish clear staff responsibility.
5. Maintain complaint history.
6. Improve student communication.
7. Capture feedback.
8. Improve administrative monitoring.

---

# 3. Business Process

The business process is:

```text
Student
   ↓
Reports Complaint
   ↓
Administrator
   ↓
Reviews Complaint
   ↓
Assigns Staff
   ↓
Staff
   ↓
Processes Complaint
   ↓
Resolves Issue
   ↓
Student
   ↓
Confirms Resolution
   ↓
Complaint Closed
   ↓
Feedback
```

---

# 4. Business Rules

### BR-01

Every complaint belongs to a student.

### BR-02

An administrator assigns complaints to staff.

### BR-03

Staff can work only on complaints assigned to them.

### BR-04

Staff cannot close complaints.

### BR-05

Students can close only their own complaints.

### BR-06

A complaint must be Resolved before student closure.

### BR-07

Closed complaints cannot receive new chat messages.

### BR-08

A complaint can have one feedback record.

### BR-09

Complaint status changes must be recorded.

### BR-10

Access to personal information is role dependent.

---

# 5. Business Requirements

| ID    | Business Requirement                    | Priority |
| ----- | --------------------------------------- | -------- |
| BR-01 | Centralized complaint registration      | High     |
| BR-02 | Staff responsibility through assignment | High     |
| BR-03 | Transparent complaint status            | High     |
| BR-04 | Complaint timeline                      | High     |
| BR-05 | Role-based information protection       | Critical |
| BR-06 | Complaint communication                 | Medium   |
| BR-07 | Student confirmation before closure     | High     |
| BR-08 | Post-resolution feedback                | Medium   |

---

# 6. Key Performance Indicators

Possible system KPIs include:

### Complaint Volume

Number of complaints submitted.

### Assignment Rate

Number of complaints that have been assigned.

### Resolution Rate

Number of complaints reaching Resolved.

### Closure Rate

Number of complaints reaching Closed.

### Resolution Time

Time between complaint creation and resolution.

### Feedback Rating

Average or distribution of student ratings.

---

# 7. Acceptance Criteria

The system will satisfy business requirements when:

1. A student can submit a complaint.
2. The complaint receives a unique complaint code.
3. Admin can assign it to staff.
4. The assigned staff member can see it.
5. Other staff members cannot access it.
6. Staff can process it.
7. Staff can mark it Resolved.
8. Student can confirm the resolution.
9. Complaint becomes Closed.
10. Student can provide feedback.
11. Unauthorized access is rejected.
12. XML export works.
13. XSD validation succeeds.
14. DTD validation succeeds.

---

# 8. Business Risks

| Risk                       | Mitigation                     |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Unauthorized access        | Server-side authorization      |
| Unclear responsibility     | Staff assignment               |
| Premature closure          | Closure restricted to Resolved |
| Lost history               | Complaint update timeline      |
| Uncontrolled communication | Complaint-specific chat        |
| Post-closure messages      | Server-side message blocking   |

---
